## Which server reaches which system

| Server | Reaches | Authorized for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `arc-1` | <system> | read and write |
| `adt-mcp-server` | <system> | read and ATC only; **not** authorized for <other system> |
| `murbani.vscode-abap-remote-fs` | <system>, <system> | read-only inspection |

## Fallbacks

When the first-choice server is not authorized for the target client, name the substitute here so
the agent switches deliberately instead of improvising:

- <client> → use <server> instead of <server>, because <reason>

## Keeping this current

The connection list (`~/.copilot/state/arc1-connections.json`) and the ABAP FS destinations in
`settings.json` are the machines' own records. This file only explains them; when they change,
update this file in the same sitting, or the agent will route by a stale map.
